11. FEATURE SIX: OPEN INNOVATION EXPLAINER
==========================================

Create a dedicated educational page titled:

"WHY THE GHOST BELONGS TO EVERYONE"

Explain open-weight AI through the actual design decisions in this project.

Discuss:

1. Privacy:
   Local inference can reduce the need to send prompts to remote services.

2. Independence:
   A local application can continue working without an internet connection after the necessary software and model files have been downloaded, provided its features do not depend on external services.

3. Adaptability:
   Developers can experiment with compatible models, prompts, and inference settings.

4. Cost:
   Local inference can avoid per-request API charges, although hardware, electricity, storage, and maintenance still have costs.

5. Longevity:
   A local application and downloadable model artifacts can reduce dependence on one hosted AI provider.

6. Transparency:
   A developer can inspect the application code and provider integration.

7. Limitations:
   Open weights do not automatically guarantee unrestricted use, complete transparency, model accuracy, privacy, or a fully open-source software stack.

Explain the differences among:

